-- statement:
--   **The exact counterpart of an axis-by-axis pass**: the base `tensorMap` of the lifted line maps is the kernel tensor `tens (kerL L)`, read on `[0, a)`-addresses and at `ĵ = j mod b`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFMLines`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFM.tensorMap_liftL {a b : Fin d → ℕ} [∀ i, NeZero (a i)] [∀ i, NeZero (b i)]
--       (L : (i : Fin d) → (ZMod (a i) → ℂ) →L[ℂ] (ZMod (b i) → ℂ))
--       (x : (Fin d → ℕ) → ℂ) (j : Fin d → ℕ) :
--       tensorMap (fun i => NLogN.KFM.liftL (L i)) x j =
--         IntMul.OpenAI.RT.tens (kerL L) (fun k => x (fun i => (k i).val)) (fun i => ((j i : ℕ) : ZMod (b i)))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *Item 12 (math side, part 2): line maps applied axis by axis*: The machine applies the per-axis fixed-point maps (`Sapprox`, `B0P`) slice by slice. That is
--   the base `tensorMapZ` (via `tensorGo_eq`, `KFMBaseTGo`). This file identifies the exact
--   counterpart, the base `tensorMap` of the lifted line maps `liftL (L i)`, with the explicit tensor
--   witness `tensCLM (kerL L)` of `KFMR19`. Then base `fp_tensor` gives the error of the whole pass.
